# This .gitignore is scoped to the Unity project only (UnityProject/).

## Unity generated folders - fully reproducible from Assets/ + ProjectSettings/
[Ll]ibrary/
[Tt]emp/
[Oo]bj/
[Bb]uild/
[Bb]uilds/
[Ll]ogs/
[Mm]emoryCaptures/
[Rr]ecordings/
[Uu]serSettings/

# Output of BuildBundle.cs (Assets/Editor/BuildBundle.cs) - regenerated on every build,
# the built bundle gets copied into XSplitScreen/xsplitscreenbundle (that copy IS tracked).
AssetBundleOutput/

# Never ignore Assets/Editor itself, only build output that can land under it
[Aa]ssets/[Ee]ditor/[Bb]uild/

# Visual Studio / Rider / VS Code generated project files - regenerated by Unity
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.csproj
*.unityproj
*.sln
*.suo
*.tmp
*.user
*.userprefs
*.pidb
*.booproj
*.svd
*.pdb
*.mdb
*.opendb
*.VC.db

# Unity3D generated meta files for the above (in case any slip through)
*.pidb.meta
*.pdb.meta
*.mdb.meta

# Unity crash logs
sysinfo.txt
*.stackdump

## Proprietary game DLLs - do NOT commit these.
# Anyone working on this project needs to source their own copy of Risk of Rain 2 and
# copy the relevant DLLs from "<RoR2 install>/Risk of Rain 2_Data/Managed/" themselves.
# NOTE: as discovered, importing the full RoR2/Assembly-CSharp DLL set directly into this
# Unity Editor project as Plugins is NOT viable - Mono's class loader hard-crashes the
# Editor on a version-layout mismatch between the game's bundled DLLs and this Editor's own
# engine modules. The prefabs in this project only use Unity's own built-in UI components
# and don't need any RoR2 types; the one script that does (SplitscreenMenuController.cs)
# references a local stand-in (BaseMainMenuScreen.cs) rather than the real game type, which
# is the same technique the original author used and the one to keep using here.
Assets/Plugins/RoR2/
